message:
Command `g++ --version | head -1; echo "---test asan with g++ on a simple heap overflow---"; cat > /tmp/ovf.cpp <<'EOF'
#include <cstdlib>
#include <cstring>
int main(int argc, char** argv){
  char* p = (char*)malloc(8);
  p[8] = 'x'; // 1 byte overflow
  free(p);
  return 0;
}
EOF
g++ -fsanitize=address -O1 -g -o /tmp/ovf /tmp/ovf.cpp && /tmp/ovf 2>&1 | head -20; echo "exit=$?"` executed with exit code 0.

